# Command palette open-lag receipt, condition 1 of 4: PALETTE CLOSED, idle.
#
# The control. Same scene, same window (1024x600, turnstone's default), same
# offline graph as the other three, so the only difference between this file
# and palette_lag_open.scn is whether the palette is open. Offline by design
# (mere:// fetches nothing), so the numbers describe the chrome path and not a
# network.
#
# MEASURED BLOCK: the trailing `settle 140`, which is 141 frames (the step
# that sets the countdown is itself a frame). The harness skips the one frame
# `log` costs and reads the 120 before it, which is why the block sits at the
# end of the file and why its length must not change without changing the
# harness table beside it.
settle 30
key escape
open mere://alpha
open mere://beta
settle 20
assert visible
assert omnibar closed
settle 140
log palette lag: closed idle sample complete
